---
/* L32 - the loss curve is the diagnostic: converging, oscillating, exploding. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L32.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of three chalk strokes on a wall: a smooth line that descends and flattens onto a ledge, a jagged line bouncing around it, and a third line shooting steeply up and off the top of the frame."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L32-fig-title L32-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L32-fig-title">Three loss curves: converging, oscillating, exploding</title>
      <desc id="L32-fig-desc">
        One plot with the step number on the horizontal axis and the loss on
        the vertical axis, holding three curves. The first curve falls
        smoothly from 0.693 and flattens low, labelled converging. The second
        bounces up and down around a floor that gets slightly lower, labelled
        oscillating. The third climbs steeply and leaves the top of the plot,
        labelled exploding. A note at the side reads that a loss column ending
        in nan means the step was far too large.
      </desc>

      <!-- the axes -->
      <g class="fig-axis">
        <path d="M56 300 H612 M56 300 V44" />
      </g>
      <text x="24" y="48" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0.7</text>
      <text x="24" y="304" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0</text>
      <text x="56" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">0</text>
      <text x="316" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">1000</text>
      <text x="588" y="320" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">2000</text>
      <text x="240" y="336" class="fig-label">step</text>

      <!-- the converging curve -->
      <g class="m-draw fig-curve fig-curve--ok" style="--m-length: 630; --m-duration: 2.2s">
        <path d="M56 92 C 140 200, 220 262, 320 278 C 420 291, 520 294, 600 295" />
      </g>
      <text x="392" y="272" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">converging</text>

      <!-- the oscillating curve -->
      <g class="fig-curve fig-curve--warn">
        <path d="M56 92 C 80 200, 100 120, 130 230 C 160 140, 190 250, 220 160 C 250 260, 280 175, 310 268 C 340 190, 370 272, 400 210 C 430 274, 460 225, 490 276 C 520 240, 550 277, 600 262" />
      </g>
      <text x="392" y="238" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">oscillating</text>

      <!-- the exploding curve -->
      <g class="fig-curve fig-curve--bad">
        <path d="M56 92 C 120 60, 190 30, 260 4" />
      </g>
      <text x="278" y="26" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">exploding</text>

      <!-- the start value -->
      <g>
        <path d="M56 92 L44 92" class="fig-tick" />
        <text x="12" y="96" class="fig-text fig-text--num fig-text--dim">0.693</text>
      </g>

      <!-- the reading of the column -->
      <g>
        <rect x="392" y="52" width="204" height="52" class="fig-panel fig-panel--ink" />
        <text x="404" y="72" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">a loss column ending</text>
        <text x="404" y="86" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">in nan: the step was</text>
        <text x="404" y="100" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">far too large</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L32</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">The shape of the loss curve tells you what the learning rate did: it converges, it oscillates around a floor, or it climbs away and ends in nan.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text--num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-axis path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-curve path {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-curve--ok {
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-curve--warn {
    stroke: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .fig-curve--bad {
    stroke: var(--color-prussian);
  }

  .fig-tick {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-panel {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule-soft);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-panel--ink {
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
